  "body": "## What changed\n\n**`tormach.cps` now states the clearance height before a section's first X/Y traverse.** This applies after a tool change, after a G30, and at the program start. An upright section first writes `G0 Z<clearance>`:\n- the clearance is the stream's `PARAM ClearancePlane`, else its `RetractPlane` (the hop, #1028);\n- it is never below the move's own Z.\n\nA stream that states neither plane is refused by name, once per program: \"first X/Y traverse ... with no clearance height stated (no ClearancePlane or RetractPlane) ...\". Indexed (4th-axis) sections keep their own order: `indexFor` lifts with G53 and turns A, and their X/Y is the turned tip. The microARC tester-kit program shows the clearance landing right after `G0 A0`.\n\n**Why (from a PathPilot Hub run, 770MX sim v2.14.4).** Hub's T4 was 5\" long, and the session's G54 Z zero sat about 4.3\" below the top of Z travel. After `G43 H4` the tip stood about 0.68\" under the part top, and the bare `G0 X.. Y..` crossed the part at that height. The user saw \"down, over, up\". #1596 re-lifts with `G53 G0 Z0` after `G43`, which covers a low stored G30. The top of travel itself can still be below clearance when the tool is long for the work offset; that is what this PR covers.\n- On a setup that can clear, the new `G0 Z` is an ordinary move down to clearance before the traverse.\n- On a setup that cannot, the control refuses that block as past its Z limit and the program stops. It no longer rapids through the part.\n\n`assets/posts/AGENTS.md` states the law.\n\n### Goldens regenerated (WRITE_GOLDEN=1); each gains exactly one `G0 Z..` line before its first X/Y traverse, nothing else\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach/`: the 13 legacy programs (`contour_disc_hole`, `contour_plate_with_hole`, `contour_tangential_lead`, `drill_peck`, `drill_plate`, `face_square_40x40`, `face_square_40x40_stepped`, `pocket_waterline_plate_with_island`, `pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island`, `slot_fullwidth_centerline`, `slot_wide_channel_rows`, `tap_plate`, `trace_plate_with_hole`), plus `index_4face_microarc4`, `probe_bore_centre`, `probe_bore_centre_mm`, `probe_boss_centre`, `probe_corner`, `probe_edge`, `probe_face` and `probe_guard_moves`.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/tormach/`: `contour_plate_with_hole`, `drill_peck`.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_tormach.nc`: `G0 Z5` (its ClearancePlane 10 minus OriginZ 5).\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/ream/tormach.nc`.\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/tormach/`: `arcs`, `drill_retract`, `extreme_coords`, `full_circle`, `full_circle_raw`, `probe`.\n- `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/microarc_test_part.nc`.\n\nThat is 32 files, 32 added lines. No snapshot PNG was touched.\n\n### Test inputs given the plane a real section carries\n- `tests/common/legacy_program.rs` `as_program` now states `PARAM ClearancePlane` from the legacy golden's `START` height.\n- These hand-written streams gain `PARAM ClearancePlane`: `tormach_post.rs`, `tormach_program_end.rs`, `tormach_routers.rs`, `tormach_safe_retract.rs`, `tormach_toolchange_lift.rs`, `tormach_fourth_axis.rs`, `post_cycle_feed_spindle.rs` and the post crate's `work_offset_index.rs`.\n- `tormach_post::the_first_move_after_a_tool_change_positions_xy_with_z_up` now asserts the new order: a Z-only `G0 Z0.3937` (the 10 mm clearance), then X/Y alone.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/post/tests/tormach_traverse_clearance.rs`)\n\n| Test | Fails when |\n|---|---|\n| `the_first_traverse_after_a_tool_change_states_the_clearance_z_first` | the `G0 Z` is removed |\n| `the_retract_plane_serves_when_no_clearance_plane_is_stated` | the `G0 Z` is removed, or the RetractPlane fallback is removed |\n| `the_traverse_is_never_below_the_moves_own_height` | the `G0 Z` is removed, or the max with the move's own Z is removed |\n| `a_first_traverse_with_no_stated_plane_is_refused_by_name` | the refusal is removed |\n\nAll four mutations were checked; each one fails the test(s) above.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post` (all debug suites) before the input and golden updates: 14 targets failed. All of it was the expected fallout listed above. After the updates every one passes.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (post suites, app suites 885 s, 0 failed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- **The Hub re-run.** The new `drill_peck` and `contour_plate_with_hole` (inch, 770MX) are in the user's hub-tests folder `1614-770MX/` for that run.\n- **The other mill posts.** They have the same pattern and are filed as **#1616** (P1, effort:high, area:post): grblhal and carvera make a bare X/Y traverse; the Fanuc family makes a combined first rapid from the tool-change height.\n- The release-lane `--ignored` suites and the UI suites (no UI code touched).\n\nChangelog: The Tormach mill post states the section's clearance Z before its first X/Y traverse after a tool change (and refuses a stream that states no clearance or retract plane), so a tool too long for the work offset stops at the control's Z limit instead of rapiding through the part.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nFixes #1614\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
